  "scenario_brief": "NPC LOCAL AVOIDANCE TEST\n\nProves that a walking NPC routes around the player and other NPCs instead of shoving into them (npc-behavior.js _handleBlockerAhead).\n\nWHAT TO WATCH:\n1. Two staff (amy_walker, zed_walker) pace the same east-west lane in opposite phase. When they meet head-on in the desk pinch they do NOT grind into each other: one gives way (the higher id, zed_walker, backs off or waits) while the other passes, then both carry on. No deadlock.\n2. Stand on the lane in front of a walker. It stops, then detours round you; it never pushes you along. Stand behind or beside it and it ignores you (the tailgate lever is intact).\n3. rob_router walks a loop through the single north doorway into the vault and back. Stand in the doorway: he waits, then (no way round a filled doorway) squeezes gently past or gives up — never a sustained shove, never jitter.\n\nTEST DURATION: 1-2 minutes. Nothing to solve.",
  "endGoal": "Observe NPCs routing around the player and each other without a sustained shove or a deadlock.",
